      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this now runs for `setNoVerify(true)` commits, `RebaseCommand` and `CherryPickCommand` can get an `AbortedByHookException` from a step that couldn\u0027t fail before, and neither handles it. In rebase the pick is already popped from the todo and `rebase-merge/message` is never written, so `--continue` fails with a `JGitInternalException` (FileNotFoundException) and only abort works. Cherry-pick leaves the picked changes staged with no CHERRY_PICK_HEAD/MERGE_MSG. Native git stops in a resumable state here. Either handle the exception there (stop like a conflict and write the message files) or keep internal commits out of this change for now?",
